## A streamlined .gitignore for modern .NET projects
## including temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular .NET tools. If you are
## developing with Visual Studio, the VS .gitignore
## https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
## has more thorough IDE-specific entries.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg

# dotenv environment variables file
.env

# Others
~$*
*~
CodeCoverage/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml
nunit-*.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LoreFetch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Card imagery must NEVER be committed. The artwork is Wizards of the Coast IP
# regardless of who photographed it, so this covers both Scryfall renders and
# our own captures. Only DERIVED data belongs in git: the hash index, the
# accuracy tables. See docs/CONTRACTS.md and CLAUDE.md.
fixtures/
corpus/
captures/
scryfall-cache/
*.card.png
*.card.jpg

# Belt-and-braces: no bare raster files anywhere in the tree. UI assets are
# added with an explicit negation below so a slip can't sneak a card through.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff

# UI/doc assets, opted in deliberately and individually.
!src/LoreFetch.App/Assets/**
!docs/img/**

# The local collection file and its backup are user data, not source.
collection.csv
collection.csv.bak

# Generated hash index is committed on purpose (derived fingerprints, ~8.2 MiB,
# no imagery) — but the raw downloads that built it are not.
scryfall-bulk/

# Local test imagery: same relative path on the Mac and the PC, never pushed.
# Everything inside is ignored (not just rasters — ground-truth CSVs name real
# cards next to real photos); only the README that explains the folder is tracked.
test-images/*
!test-images/README.md

# Linked worktrees only — a `git add -A` on main must never pick up a worktree
# as an embedded repository.
#
# Everything else under .claude/ IS tracked, deliberately and for one reason:
# Claude Code runs on both the Mac and the Windows PC against this same repo,
# and in four linked worktrees after the fork. skills/ only apply where they
# exist on disk, so git is the only thing that puts them on the other machine. A skill that lives in one checkout is a
# skill the other machine silently does not have.
#
# The consequence to respect: this repo is PUBLIC, so .claude/skills/ holds
# project skills only. Nothing personal and nothing work-related goes there.
.claude/worktrees/
.idea/
# Personal Rider run configuration; kept local, not shared.
.run/LoreFetch.App.run.xml

# macOS directory metadata.
.DS_Store

# Demo video: script, deck layout and assets (local only)
docs/demo/
